    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sorry, I was just picturing the little gremlin inside the compressor—the one who's supposed to spin the fan but has given up. No actual goblins, I promise. Just a mechanical one.\n\nYes, it can be dangerous if you leave it humming. The motor is drawing current but not turning, so it will overheat and could burn out the windings or even start a small electrical fire. It's like a goblin who keeps pulling the bellows but forgets to open the flue—eventually the whole forge gets too hot.\n\nSo don't run it. Kill the breaker, and if you're not comfortable testing the capacitor or checking the motor, call an HVAC tech. They'll have the right tools and know how to avoid the goblin's trap—which, in this case, is a charged capacitor that can bite you even with the power off.",
